    "cost_closing_html":  "\u003cp\u003eThat is about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) versus \u003cstrong\u003e$9 or more\u003c/strong\u003e for a green-chile burrito out. The potato is what keeps this one cheap and filling at the same time.\u003c/p\u003e",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTurkey and potatoes are the cheap muscle here.\u003c/strong\u003e A pound and a quarter of russets bulks out the filling for almost nothing and carries the green chile flavor. Dice them small so they cook through with the meat.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned green chiles bring the whole profile.\u003c/strong\u003e A couple of 4 ounce cans give you the roasted chile note across all 14 burritos without a trip to a specialty store.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSalsa keeps it a burrito, not a wet mess.\u003c/strong\u003e One jar seasons and moistens the filling while it stays wrappable. Buy the medium and adjust the heat with the green chiles."
